{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas` skill MUST be the home of routing tasks to skills, `habeas status` and `habeas info`, directive and reference syntax, distributed requirements, and gotchas common to every task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The one marked test, `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_habeas_skill_is_home_of_routing_inspection_syntax_and_shared_gotchas]`, adequately checks `requirements.cli.skill_structure.habeas`. The requirement says the `habeas` skill MUST be the home of five topics. Under the parent `requirements.cli.skill_structure`, each topic must also be stated in full in exactly one skill.\n\nMapping obligations to assertions:\n- **Routing tasks to skills.** The test asserts that the `## Workflow` section of `SKILL.md` contains the `| Task | Skill |` table. `bundled_skill_workflows_end_by_naming_the_skill_for_the_next_task` (marked for `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.next`) also checks that the table names every other skill.\n- **`habeas status` and `habeas info`.** The test asserts that the `## Inspecting` section contains `` `habeas status [<selection>]` `` and `` `habeas info <selection>` ``.\n- **Directive syntax.** The test asserts that `## Requirements, examples, and definitions` covers the fenced `{req}`, `{example}` and `{definition}` directives.\n- **Reference syntax.** The test asserts that `## References` covers writing a reference in a source comment and fencing a reference. It also asserts that `references/syntax-details.md` has the \"Full names in nested chapters\" and \"Anchors\" sections.\n- **Distributed requirements.** The test asserts that `references/distributed-requirements.md` exists and has the `# Distributed requirements` heading. The `assert_home` markers also include the site-query and `{violations}` text.\n- **Gotchas common to every task.** The test asserts that `## Gotchas` mentions that reference discovery uses the Git index. The `assert_home` markers add further gotchas: a directive that silently defines nothing, the longer outer fence, and the disposable artifacts under the Cargo target directory.\n- **Exactly one home.** `assert_home(\"habeas\")` does two things:\n  - It uses `assert_phrases` to check that the habeas skill, including its reference files, contains each marker in `home_markers(\"habeas\")`.\n  - It loops over the other four skills (`habeas-requirements`, `habeas-evidence`, `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, `habeas-refactor`) and asserts that none of them contains any of those markers.\n\nThe markers cover the routing table, selection and glob semantics, nested chapter naming, fenced references, `{violations}`, site queries, and the gotchas. A skill that dropped a topic, or that restated it in full elsewhere, would fail the test.\n\nThe assertions are phrase-based, which fits a requirement about skill text. They check both presence in the home skill and absence from the other skills. I found no unacknowledged gap. The surrounding tests for related requirements (`skill_structure`, `skill_structure.refer`, `cli.info`) are separate obligations and aren't needed here.",
  "references": "3e613787d62d50092286fd528020c2381ceb86235c44291883f55c4a6d9690e7",
